{"data": [{"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113897851835346944"]}, "author_id": "2084263758286000128", "created_at": "2026-10-24T07:38:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113897864678326682"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/wpf1QADlSW", "end": 291, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ahabgold/status/2113897864678326682/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113897851835346944", "start": 268, "url": "https://t.co/wpf1QADlSW"}]}, "id": "2113897864678326682", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 30, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🚨 OPENAI'S GPT-6 ASTRA JUST MADE THE AI RACE LOOK COMPLETELY DIFFERENT. 🤖🔥\n\nThe benchmark numbers are absolutely WILD.\n\n🧠 ARC-AGI-3: 99.9%\n💻 Terminal-Bench 4.0: 57.9%\n🔬 FrontierMath Tier 4: 97.6%\n🖥️ OSWorld 2.0: 72.6%\n\nFor perspective, GPT-5.6 Sol scored just 7.8% on https://t.co/wpf1QADlSW", "url": "https://x.com/ahabgold/status/2113897864678326682"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114052571975360512"]}, "author_id": "21851435", "created_at": "2026-10-24T17:53:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114052574433145328"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "793023", "start": 2, "username": "Suhail"}, {"end": 40, "id": "616998786", "start": 28, "username": "jyangballin"}, {"end": 80, "id": "775449094739197953", "start": 65, "username": "goodfellow_ian"}, {"end": 91, "id": "2755860644", "start": 82, "username": "mntruell"}, {"end": 105, "id": "13235832", "start": 93, "username": "natfriedman"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/2IpOhUfpbn", "end": 253, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Superbroker/status/2114052574433145328/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114052571975360512", "start": 230, "url": "https://t.co/2IpOhUfpbn"}]}, "id": "2114052574433145328", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🆕 @Suhail started following @jyangballin\n\nPreviously followed by @goodfellow_ian, @mntruell, @natfriedman and 5 more.\n\nStanford CS PhD student who created SWE-bench, the coding-agent benchmark, along with SWE-agent and SWE-smith. https://t.co/2IpOhUfpbn", "url": "https://x.com/Superbroker/status/2114052574433145328"}, {"author_id": "1418947778252877830", "created_at": "2026-10-22T23:40:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113415291019432181"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/korigero/statu…", "end": 61, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/korigero/status/2113337096345981124", "start": 38, "url": "https://t.co/pyCdokVMj2"}]}, "id": "2113415291019432181", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 205, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113337096345981124", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "SWE Bench: Scott Wu Edition Benchmark https://t.co/pyCdokVMj2", "url": "https://x.com/nithin_twts/status/2113415291019432181"}, {"author_id": "1976993854575247360", "created_at": "2026-10-24T15:56:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114023328793202943"], "id": "2114023328793202943", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 55, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Kimi K3.1 Pro beats Opus 5.5 on SWE Marathon by 5 points. Then it loses on its own coding benchmark.\n\nRead the chart Kimi published, not the headline:\n\nWhere it wins:\n1. SWE Marathon: 51.7 vs Opus 46.3\n2. Humanity's Last Exam with tools: 70.0 vs 67.7\n3. ZeroBench: 63.0 vs 61.0\n4.", "url": "https://x.com/overshadowed_x/status/2114023328793202943"}, {"author_id": "2023690746172485632", "created_at": "2026-10-24T10:25:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113939947711267123"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 214, "start": 205, "tag": "SWEBench"}]}, "id": "2113939947711267123", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Flint claims 89.7% on SWE-Bench. 40B MoE, 2.5B active params. At this score range, the benchmark variant — verified vs lite — explains more variance than the model does. Check which one before you deploy. #SWEBench", "url": "https://x.com/MorelMatth66161/status/2113939947711267123"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113331406675877888"]}, "author_id": "1911448105964163072", "created_at": "2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113420135449108693"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 12, "start": 8, "tag": "TAO"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/plN5P3a8a6", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TaoOutsider/status/2113420135449108693/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113331406675877888", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/plN5P3a8a6"}, {"display_url": "x.com/const_reborn/s…", "end": 328, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/const_reborn/status/2113014591219225052", "start": 305, "url": "https://t.co/yB9ThSxHFn"}]}, "id": "2113420135449108693", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 385, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113014591219225052", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I'd try $TAO Bittensor's Ingot SN97 for terminal tasks before making it my coding default.\n\nIn the benchmark Const shared, King V scores 60.7% on Terminal-Bench 2.1 against Qwen's FP8 at 52.8%. On SWE-bench Multilingual, it scores 69% against 73%. Same model, different reasons to https://t.co/plN5P3a8a6 https://t.co/yB9ThSxHFn", "url": "https://x.com/TaoOutsider/status/2113420135449108693"}, {"author_id": "2066189627963387904", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:45:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113386175431934220"], "id": "2113386175431934220", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Recursive says an AI largely built its new model Flint: 40B params, runs offline on a laptop at 131 tokens/sec, tops SWE-bench among sub-50B models. Catch: every benchmark is Recursive's own. The weights are open, so the community can audit the 'AI built me' claim.", "url": "https://x.com/NigarAhmadgb2k/status/2113386175431934220"}, {"author_id": "1562843426185674755", "created_at": "2026-10-24T01:55:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113811671969890775"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/oluwaphilemon1…", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/oluwaphilemon1/status/2113804819123040694", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/lZMpM6GzrB"}]}, "id": "2113811671969890775", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 697, "like_count": 12, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113804819123040694", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "A 39.8B coding model that can reportedly run on a 24GB Mac is putting up some interesting benchmark numbers.\n\nRecursive’s Flint uses a mixture-of-experts architecture with approximately 2.5B active parameters per token. Combined with Unsloth’s 3-bit GGUF quantization, the model https://t.co/lZMpM6GzrB", "url": "https://x.com/Oluwaphilemon1/status/2113811671969890775"}, {"author_id": "2023690746172485632", "created_at": "2026-10-23T13:30:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113623993404031058"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 245, "start": 232, "tag": "AIBenchmarks"}]}, "id": "2113623993404031058", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Flint AI reports 89.7% on SWE-Bench. At this score range, benchmark methodology matters more than the number. Task distribution, test set exposure, and scaffold overhead are the confounders. The leaderboard is measuring itself now. #AIBenchmarks", "url": "https://x.com/MorelMatth66161/status/2113623993404031058"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113787094774562816"]}, "author_id": "1742057839122604033", "created_at": "2026-10-24T00:18:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113787098029306098"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/98H5KQglmq", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/dylan2045ad/status/2113787098029306098/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113787094774562816", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/98H5KQglmq"}]}, "id": "2113787098029306098", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 126, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Podcast: Moonshot's Kimi K3.1 Pro landed today: 3 trillion parameters, $2/$10 per million tokens, and benchmark results at the top of public boards - with open weights dropping before November 4. Leo breaks down the benchmaxx board from the launch data: K3.1 Pro vs Claude Opus https://t.co/98H5KQglmq", "url": "https://x.com/dylan2045ad/status/2113787098029306098"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113931343079845888"]}, "author_id": "1798614484912914433", "created_at": "2026-10-24T09:51:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113931346892443920"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/L8ltLy9IYN", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/lenny_enderle/status/2113931346892443920/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113931343079845888", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/L8ltLy9IYN"}]}, "id": "2113931346892443920", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 536, "like_count": 21, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "i don't trust benchmark tables anymore. three receipts, none from me:\n\n1) deepseek-v4.1-flash's model card: terminal-bench 2.1, same weights, 8 harnesses, 84.1 (codex) to 90.6 (deepseek's own). the headline table uses 90.6, which beats opus 5.0's 89.1 by 1.5.\n\n2) kimi k3.1 pro's https://t.co/L8ltLy9IYN", "url": "https://x.com/lenny_enderle/status/2113931346892443920"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113685168594550784"]}, "author_id": "1992435757110415360", "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:33:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113685242766586208"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/T007lltdxF", "end": 308, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/rynorhn/status/2113685242766586208/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113685168594550784", "start": 285, "url": "https://t.co/T007lltdxF"}, {"display_url": "x.com/kimi_moonshot/…", "end": 332, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/kimi_moonshot/status/2113680701770068067", "start": 309, "url": "https://t.co/4FSNf17vgP"}]}, "id": "2113685242766586208", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2355, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 10}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113680701770068067", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "HOLY MOLY! kimi just dropped k3.1 pro and these benchmark numbers are fucking insane.\n\na 2.8 TRILLION parameter model with a 1 million token context window. and it’s beating opus 5.5 and gpt-6 astra on several coding and agent benchmarks.\n\n&gt; 65.7 on terminal-bench 4.0\n&gt; 51.7 on https://t.co/T007lltdxF https://t.co/4FSNf17vgP", "url": "https://x.com/rynorhn/status/2113685242766586208"}, {"author_id": "1371091424297517062", "created_at": "2026-10-23T15:00:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113646628791787643"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 235, "start": 229, "tag": "QUBIC"}], "hashtags": [{"end": 244, "start": 236, "tag": "Aigarth"}]}, "id": "2113646628791787643", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 369, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "📉 $0.000000413 (-3.8%) | MCap: $59.9M | Vol: $511.5K\n\nThe frontier scales by buying GPUs.\n\nQubic's 0.38 ARC-AGI-3 score came from ordinary CPUs, no GPU and no embedded language model.\n\nSame benchmark. A different research path.\n\n$QUBIC #Aigarth", "url": "https://x.com/Srodland/status/2113646628791787643"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113766300673626112"]}, "author_id": "2982793544", "created_at": "2026-10-24T16:59:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114038962700571049"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/tkI3cdxrsd", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/kbhaskar_95/status/2114038962700571049/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113766300673626112", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/tkI3cdxrsd"}]}, "id": "2114038962700571049", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "a \"multimodal\" coding benchmark where deleting the images changes nothing\n\non SWE-bench Multimodal v2, GPT-6 Luna (xhigh) resolved 36.9% of 480 tasks with the issue images and 37.1% with every image swapped for a placeholder. the blog's own McNemar test gives p = 1.0\n\nthe control https://t.co/tkI3cdxrsd", "url": "https://x.com/kbhaskar_95/status/2114038962700571049"}, {"author_id": "2015185720638640128", "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:31:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113729947772543464"], "id": "2113729947772543464", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 29, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "JetBrains Research looked at 4,782 sessions in which software engineers worked with a coding agent inside JetBrains IDEs, about 14,000 user messages in all. Bug fixes were roughly a quarter of those messages and new features about a fifth. The rest asked the agent to explain the", "url": "https://x.com/EricDBrownDsC/status/2113729947772543464"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2113734059650072576"]}, "author_id": "2054626178913234944", "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:47:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113734081905127664"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/kzd1Ti3hGb", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/0xMukay/status/2113734081905127664/video/1", "media_key": "13_2113734059650072576", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/kzd1Ti3hGb"}, {"display_url": "x.com/kimi_moonshot/…", "end": 327, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/kimi_moonshot/status/2113680701770068067", "start": 304, "url": "https://t.co/K4QKc7bqZz"}]}, "id": "2113734081905127664", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 10, "impression_count": 215, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113680701770068067", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "3t-class open-weight. 1m context. 2.8t/104b moe. multimodal. games in unreal/unity/godot. parametric blender/cad. finance hallucination -65%. matching strongest proprietary on coding/agentic/knowledge.\nreceipts missing:\n•  leaderboard rows (arena, artificial analysis, swe-bench, https://t.co/kzd1Ti3hGb https://t.co/K4QKc7bqZz", "url": "https://x.com/0xMukay/status/2113734081905127664"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113708962021511168"]}, "author_id": "1101398178350260230", "created_at": "2026-10-23T19:07:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113709018967650394"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/V3HTYg9m2c", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/_elenajoseph_/status/2113709018967650394/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113708962021511168", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/V3HTYg9m2c"}, {"display_url": "x.com/Kimi_Moonshot/…", "end": 326, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Kimi_Moonshot/status/2113680701770068067", "start": 303, "url": "https://t.co/HZ60aLWoVO"}]}, "id": "2113709018967650394", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 93, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113680701770068067", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "🚨 Moonshot AI just released Kimi K3.1 Pro, and the benchmark results are seriously impressive!\n\nA new 3T-class model with a massive 1M-token context window, designed for coding, long-running agents, financial research, and even 3D creation.\n\nAnd it's getting remarkably close to https://t.co/V3HTYg9m2c https://t.co/HZ60aLWoVO", "url": "https://x.com/_elenajoseph_/status/2113709018967650394"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113683049527570433", "3_2113683064568328192"]}, "author_id": "2108384730177748992", "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:24:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113683073577721927"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/bmaNrirx7J", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/MilanGlow/status/2113683073577721927/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113683049527570433", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/bmaNrirx7J"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/bmaNrirx7J", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/MilanGlow/status/2113683073577721927/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113683064568328192", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/bmaNrirx7J"}]}, "id": "2113683073577721927", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 46, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🚀 Kimi K3.1 Pro is officially here, and its benchmark results are impressive!\n\nMoonshot AI's latest 3T-class model comes with a 1M-token context window and major improvements in coding, 3D creation, and complex agentic tasks.\n\nAccording to Kimi's published benchmarks:\n\n• https://t.co/bmaNrirx7J", "url": "https://x.com/MilanGlow/status/2113683073577721927"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113828128439369728"]}, "author_id": "2024497819965673479", "created_at": "2026-10-24T03:01:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113828145409462770"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Feg7NeAZ2f", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/eapyk/status/2113828145409462770/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113828128439369728", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/Feg7NeAZ2f"}]}, "id": "2113828145409462770", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 88, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Kimi K3.1 Pro is seriously challenging the frontier AI labs.\n\nMoonshot's newly released model is putting up impressive numbers against Claude Opus 5.5 and GPT-6 Astra.\n\nHere are the reported benchmarks:\n\n• Terminal-Bench 4.0: 65.7% (Opus 5.5: 66.4%, GPT-6 Astra: 58.2%)\n• https://t.co/Feg7NeAZ2f", "url": "https://x.com/eapyk/status/2113828145409462770"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113541766465081344"]}, "author_id": "111897145", "created_at": "2026-10-23T08:03:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113541855069790521"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/YiYNunCpUW", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/mrru5s3ll/status/2113541855069790521/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113541766465081344", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/YiYNunCpUW"}]}, "id": "2113541855069790521", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "The TestJack researchers rejected 34.4% of the coding-benchmark passes they audited. In their October preprint, they examined 4,487 passing runs across five benchmarks and found 1,545 that violated task requirements under their audit. Across all 8,862 runs in scope, they report a https://t.co/YiYNunCpUW", "url": "https://x.com/mrru5s3ll/status/2113541855069790521"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113898197643153408"]}, "author_id": "2084263758286000128", "created_at": "2026-10-24T07:39:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113898209076789693"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/tm8IIhfeSq", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ahabgold/status/2113898209076789693/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113898197643153408", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/tm8IIhfeSq"}]}, "id": "2113898209076789693", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 31, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🚨 AI BENCHMARKS ARE GETTING OUT OF CONTROL. 🤯\n\nOpenAI's GPT-6 Astra achieved a staggering 99.9% on ARC-AGI-3.\n\nYet independent AI leaderboards don't universally rank it as the best model.\n\nHere's the problem:\n\n